    "title": "Count bites or sips with 口",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-mouthful-count-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Count bites or sips with 口",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "After 吃 or 喝, number + 口 counts bites or sips. This differs from 家有三口人, which counts household members.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我喝了一口水。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ hē le yī kǒu shuǐ 。",
                "meaning": "I took one sip of water.",
                "audio": "86382ed96f77d2a09b0a1565d625a7b26059f80266100e68fd6fa76f151f27e2"
              },
              {
                "text": "他吃了两口饭。",
                "pinyin": "tā chī le liǎng kǒu fàn 。",
                "meaning": "He ate two mouthfuls of rice.",
                "audio": "32e8c2fba7ab5a203b98e57a5be052f3c4df72d7334b5f4cc6fef07e33572b47"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
